// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 14 „Ühiskond ja avalikud teenused” (b1b2-066…070), stage B2.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, the cast a year after the B1 course
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): in Viktor's village in Kõrvemaa the family doctor's office was closed and moved 30 km away
// (Viktor, 64, no car, a bad knee); Olena (from Harkiv, was an accountant, now a shop assistant) waits half a year for
// a free B1 language course and applies to Nõmme for course support; Liis volunteers (food bank, a language café in the
// library, clean-up days) and speaks on Ülle's radio show „Päevateema” with Olena; Nõmme's participatory budget
// (kaasav eelarve: skate park, community garden, playground — Sofia and Markus help Liis's team); in Anna's block of
// flats in Saue (housing association Pärna 12, board chair Tarmo, neighbours Maire and Heino) a new house order is
// set and the newcomer Igor (came to Estonia half a year ago, works in the Tuul Logistika warehouse) asks what is
// compulsory; before the local elections candidates Margit Allik and Toomas Sepp debate the dangerous school street at
// Kase kool (host Hannes); Liis and Jaan bring a proposal to the Nõmme district commission (member Jüri Mänd).
// New people: valla esindaja Olga (focus group, picture 066), sotsiaaltöötaja Tiiu Raud, infotelefon Kertu.
// One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner presents a local problem's solution to the Nõmme district
// commission and writes a formal application (069 Kasuta).
// Grammar (B2, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5, spiral): the impersonal in official texts (suleti, on viidud,
// on kehtestatud, ei leitud; total object in the nominative) — 066 (notice, rule table, transformation, used in the
// social-worker meeting and the letter); government (rektsioon) of civic verbs (osalema milles, panustama millesse,
// taotlema mida, kaebama kelle peale / mille üle, pöörduma kelle poole, vastutama mille eest, sõltuma millest) —
// 067 (notice, categorize by case, gaps, the application text); participles and non-finite clauses in rules
// (on kohustatud / keelatud / lubatud, kehtestatud kord, selleks ettenähtud, rikkumise korral, -des, -mata) — 068 (notice,
// rule table, transformation, participle forms, the sentence-bank text, the board letter); all three come back in 069
// (the commission's reply, error correction, the proposal and the formal application) with the conditional of a
// proposal (maksaks, suletaks, riskiks oleks).
// The final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 14, 2026-10-29): 066 RÄÄK R→S (corner W1 = the 80–100-word
// e-mail to the social worker, W08; main = S10 meeting with the social worker), 067 LUGE R→W (corner R1 = the problem
// article „Kaasav eelarve: kas iga hääl loeb?”, ≈ 500 words; main = W14 post to the neighbours with a counter-argument),
// 068 PROJ L→S (corner L1 = ten short announcements played once, L01; main = S16 talk at the general meeting, recorded
// at home), 069 KIRJ L→W (corner W2a = the board survey chart summarised with a comment, W15; main = W13 formal
// application). Every teaching lesson: review naming the previous lesson and a module 10–12 lesson, a pair task in the
// lesson, a home recording in Kasuta (S15 / S16), two fluency tasks; S16 in 068, S17 in 068 and 069. Module 13's words
// return: keskkond, jäätmed, sorteerima, heitmed, ühistransport, kulu, mõju, lahendus, ettepanek, elanik, vald.
//   066 the focus-group article (predict and check); Olena's call to the language-course line; the district notice
//       (cloze); Viktor's meeting with the social worker Tiiu Raud, a voice message to Sofia, an e-mail to Tiiu.
//   067 Ülle's radio show with Liis and Olena (short answers); the participatory-budget article; Olena's application
//       for course support (forms); the three ideas, Sofia and Markus choose, a speech recorded at home, a post.
//   068 the Pärna 12 house order; ten short announcements; advice for newcomers (sentence bank); the board's stricter
//       proposals, argument cards at the general meeting, Anna's talk, Igor's draft rewritten for the board.
//   069 the candidates' debate; the board questionnaire; a youth council's sample proposal (paragraphs shuffled) and the
//       commission's reply; the pro / contra debate and the survey summary; Jüri Mänd's voice message, the presentation
//       recorded at home, the commission's questions, the application.
// Lesson 5 (070) is the module's check in Harno B2 form: listening L3, L4; reading R1, R2a, R2b; writing W1, W2a;
// speaking S1, S2; every part timed with B.examPart. The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module14.js.
